post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

One command finishes the setup - it picks a speech model, starts the server, and
reads your keys off the keyboard so no keycode is ever typed by hand:

  talkey-setup

Safe to re-run, and `talkey-setup keys` rebinds whenever you like.

Rather do it by hand? Every step is in /usr/share/doc/talkey-git/README.md.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Note: ~/.config/i3/talkey.conf is your copy - this upgrade did not touch it.
Compare it against /usr/share/talkey/bindings/i3.conf if bindings changed, or
re-run `talkey-setup keys` to regenerate it.
EOF
}
